{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact history-design draft1 3ff9a19448e8d9df2f90dc24ce4c49ea9bb6c2b7, primary e3c388df487c9684f03cc95505466d5da80553d7. Primary read first in full; governing c98b5c99 and direct promise ee0166f1 inspected, assigned review binding verified. Six findings follow together. These are design counterexamples at cited Main7a148325, not claims that a proposed gate or refactor has already failed.\n\n1. P1 — Make cohort promotion depend on the host/client/replay predicate migration (note82,325-326). H4 makes register17/directory16/rules10/destination12 the ordinary default, while H5 is later and repairs the literal lists. At the intermediate H4 tree, Scope reads.ts219 excludes destination12 from reservationExpiry; Page src/data.ts461 accepts a proposal's published rules only for rules1-4 and returns null for rules10; CLI commands.ts1523 only selects the manifest-source edit flow for destination3-6; Replay verify.ts1671 only enters its publish-file application-origin check for destination4-7. The note already identifies these incomplete lists. Promoting the cohort before fixing and checking the corresponding paths makes omitted behavior the ordinary path. Move capability predicates and their owning native/CLI/Page/replay acceptance before, or atomically with, the default switch. Preserve each pin's exact policy; sharing destinationRules4 does not make its distinct applicationPublicationOrigin callbacks interchangeable.\n\n2. P2 — Separate retirement of new-cohort options from retained install custody (note85,325). At cited Main, commands.ts397-398 defines selectedPlan by the same INSTALL_COHORTS set that supplies fresh creation choices; executePlannedInstall at544 uses it to decide strictCustody, and 578-582 chooses verified save/readback from it before sending. Removing eleven old choices/exports without a transition for saved plans can reclassify a retained old selected-cohort plan as legacy, bypassing those custody checks, or strand an already-attempted exact request. Decide explicitly: keep exact old plan recognition/recovery through the versions table, or refuse retired plans without signing/sending/replacing or erasing their evidence. Do not conflate permission to create a new old room with classification of retained attempted/acknowledged custody. Name a saved old-plan/restart/readback-refusal witness at the transition.\n\n3. P1 — Protect executable version semantics as well as data hashes (note264-270,87-88). versions.test.ts102 hashes only supplied.data. VERSION_DATA additionally selects rules, observed/observedValues, membership/rulesScope, declaredText, hostPreparationKinds, receiverIdentity and applicationPublicationOrigin. For example changing destination9's archiveApplicationPublicationOrigin binding to another callback leaves its golden data digest unchanged while changing admission/replay meaning. That is precisely a risk when splitting/moving shared historical code and redirecting many fixture cohorts. The named A2 archive cases use fixture-specific definitions/stand-in authority and do not establish every shipped platform callback mapping. Keep all62 literal data hashes, but also specify how the exact per-pin rule/policy mappings and old-version behavioral witnesses are preserved and checked, with representative native/replay cases for the moved special policies. Do not move an old-version regression onto CURRENT merely because it uses an older cohort as a fixture if it is the witness of that older policy.\n\n4. P2 — Define file classes and history-internal edges before enforcing the history gate (note193-206,241-249). Three concrete conflicts exist in the written policy. (a) Only a versions table may import history, but historical modules depend on other historical modules and the tests moved to history/test must reach their implementation; bytes and lane history have no versions table specified. State allowed history-to-history/test edges and the exact external entrypoint rule. (b) Every history file gets a // marker, but H6 moves committed canonical lane JSON there; prefixing that strict JSON makes JSON.parse fail and changes pinned physical bytes. Use format-safe metadata/sidecars or exemptions, keeping canonical bytes exact. This also applies to a historical service config rather than a platform definition. (c) Rule5 exempts platform/tests/manifest but not records, and rule6 covers history nested inside active packages. At this exact base,31 Markdown records contain platform version literals; the promised untouched historical record remains a gate rejection. Define classification precedence and limit active naming rules to the intended source classes, with explicit fixture/record/history treatment. Name a few meaningful allowed/refused examples so the gate can enforce the design without rewriting historical records or corrupting pinned inputs.\n\n5. P2 — Include current guide migration in H2, not just tests and APPLICATION.md (note127,323). docs/write-an-application.md21/132/185-187 actively sends new authors to definition.ts, definition.test.ts, definition.json and pin.ts, all deleted by H2. docs/what-is-dap.md150 and docs/roadmap.md310 also link that definition. The note's first-reader goal is not met by leaving these links and instructions pointing at removed examples. Move these current guides to the actual commitments example in the same slice and update its semantic instructions, with a relative-link check. There are seven linked lines across the three guides, beyond the eight test consumers already inventoried. This needs no hosted-room compatibility decision and keeps H2 independently useful.\n\n6. P2 — Assign the parallel-form disposition to an executable slice and define its boundary (note94-96 versus slices322-328). The disposition promises to consolidate application-install and bytes application/package/types v1/v2 forms, but no H slice names the bytes codec work or its public export/dispatch transition. H4 is platform pins/cohorts/tests; H5 is external version questions; H6 is lanes/config. In addition, the current v2 package reader itself reuses application-package-validation's v1 semantic/presentation/release helpers (application-package-v2.ts6-8,30-31), and current platform install code uses both forms. Classify shared current implementation separately from the superseded public codec, specify the bytes history entrypoint/dispatch for retained packets and callers, and assign that work and its existing exact v1/v2 packet/retained-input witnesses to a slice. Keep signed release domains and canonical bytes unchanged; renaming a code file must not silently upgrade stored packets. It can follow H1/H2 without delaying them.\n\nInventory verification: the62 shipped pin golden rows and holes,12 cohort constants,45 dated notes,35 numbered plans,202 implementation/43report/15review files, install source line counts314/52/85/7, lane source1696/106 and seven non-record spike references match cited Main. Correct the relocated Page citation at note76 to apps/room/page/src/data.ts:461; packages/page/src/data.ts does not exist there. The handoff log has5,347 split lines (5,346 newline bytes), so its displayed count is convention-dependent, not a blocker. No product-name or article-attribution objection. H1/H2 can remain first after the scoped fixes above; no permission to re-found/delete live pins or implement/deploy follows from this design review.\n\nRead-only exact Git material and static design checks retained in /private/tmp/checker-history-d1-46ipdes8, permanently frozen after CLOSED-MANIFEST. No project/compiler/native/browser tests or gate ran for this document-only candidate; whitespace diff check0. No source/ref edit, merge, push, remote query, dependency install or deployment. Complete fresh source review required for any revised exact head.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e3c388df487c9684f03cc95505466d5da80553d7","binding":"assigned","head":"3ff9a19448e8d9df2f90dc24ce4c49ea9bb6c2b7","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c39189ffd5ae12ca84467e11465a508ab953a8ac\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ee0166f1b68f8a2aa8126f0cc37d4651fc8cfb88\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ae47cf6fd511ff2559ed2a3f562bd04bd998d3e6","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}